Bind the pad by default, and let Options open the menu.

The engine reports every pad button, stick direction and trigger as a `PAD0_*` key
(`engine/code/sdl/sdl_input.c`), and `baseq3r/default.cfg` binds none of them: a player
holding only a pad could drive the menus and nothing else. This adds racing defaults:

    R2 accelerate, L2 brake/reverse, left stick or D-pad steer,
    Cross handbrake, Square fire, Circle use item, Triangle turbo,
    L1/R1 previous/next weapon, R3 horn, Create scores, Options the menu.

They are defaults. Setup, Controls rebinds them, and a saved q3config.cfg wins.

Options is bound to `togglemenu`, which runs even while the menu is up
(`CL_BindUICommand`). The menus also took Options as "select"
(`Menu_IsGamepadSelectKey`), so one press would have both selected an item and left
the menu. Select is Cross alone now, and Options behaves as Escape everywhere: it
opens the menu in a race and backs out of one.

--- a/baseq3r/default.cfg
+++ b/baseq3r/default.cfg
@@ -37,4 +37,22 @@
 bind MOUSE4 "stoprecord"
 bind MOUSE5 "record"
 bind MWHEELDOWN "weapnext"
-bind MWHEELUP "weapprev"
\ No newline at end of file
+bind MWHEELUP "weapprev"
+//
+// The pad (PAD0_* keys; the triggers and stick directions arrive as keys too)
+//
+bind PAD0_RIGHTTRIGGER "+forward"
+bind PAD0_LEFTTRIGGER "+back"
+bind PAD0_LEFTSTICK_LEFT "+left"
+bind PAD0_LEFTSTICK_RIGHT "+right"
+bind PAD0_DPAD_LEFT "+left"
+bind PAD0_DPAD_RIGHT "+right"
+bind PAD0_A "+button14"
+bind PAD0_X "+attack"
+bind PAD0_B "+button2"
+bind PAD0_Y "+speed"
+bind PAD0_LEFTSHOULDER "weapprev"
+bind PAD0_RIGHTSHOULDER "weapnext"
+bind PAD0_RIGHTSTICK_CLICK "+button3"
+bind PAD0_BACK "+scores"
+bind PAD0_START "togglemenu"
--- a/engine/code/q3_ui/ui_qmenu.c
+++ b/engine/code/q3_ui/ui_qmenu.c
@@ -2107,7 +2107,7 @@
 
 static qboolean Menu_IsGamepadSelectKey( int key )
 {
-	if ( key == K_PAD0_A || key == K_PAD0_START ) {
+	if ( key == K_PAD0_A ) {
 		return qtrue;
 	}
 
